{
  "slug": "artist:central-cee",
  "name": "Central Cee",
  "editorial_article": "Born Oakley Neil Caesar-Su in 1998, this Shepherd's Bush native rose to prominence during the 2020 lockdown with the UK drill singles 'Day in the Life' and 'Loading'. After an early career performing trapwave and auto-tuned hip-hop, he transitioned to a melodic, upbeat approach to UK drill that secured his 2021 debut mixtape 'Wild West' a number two spot on the UK Albums Chart. His second mixtape '23', released in 2022, reached number one, while his 2023 collaboration with Dave on 'Sprinter' broke records as the longest-running number-one rap single in UK history. Central Cee has garnered international recognition through partnerships with Lil Baby on 'Band4Band', which charted at number 18 on the Billboard Hot 100, and his 2025 debut studio album 'Can't Rush Greatness', which entered the Billboard 200 at number nine. Beyond music, he founded the streetwear brand Syna World in 2023, utilizing guerrilla marketing techniques that earned comparisons to labels like Corteiz and Trapstar.",
